// Custom (non-traditional) key signature at the line start — D major's two sharps
// written as `key custom`. Pins the reserve/draw unification: the reservation reads the
// key's INK width (SpacingRules.KeySignatureInkWidth, the same model the drawn signature
// uses), so the meter and first note sit exactly where a standard D major puts them.
// Before the fix the springs reserved NO key column (the reservation read .Sharps only,
// and a custom key is KeySignature(0, custom)), so the drawn meter overlapped the first
// note. LilyPond twin: \set Staff.keyAlterations = #`((3 . ,SHARP) (0 . ,SHARP)) — its
// geometry is byte-identical to \key d \major (ledger
// line-start.time-to-first-note.custom-key, probe score KCC).
title "Custom Key"

octave absolute
time 4/4
key custom fis cis

part melody

phrase p1 {
  d4 e fis g | a4 b cis' d' |
}

section Main {
  melody { p1 }
}

form main { Main }

score main "custom-key" {
  staff melody
}
